# changelog

## 2026-08-02

- 完成 `BULK_EPOCH` 固定30篇真实 A/B 验收：正式 R2 单文档与跨文档均 30/30 成功，M1/M2/M3/M4 并发 8/24/24/12 下墙钟环比下降 21.90%、总 Token 下降 1.97%、N9 Input 下降 58.76%；但高置信 Package Gold 子集的 Pair Precision/Recall 从 87.99%/78.81% 降至 82.57%/32.95%，碎片 excess components 从 3 增至 16。结论为保留 epoch、幂等、并发 lane、N9 组件化与完整 N13 finalize，但下一轮必须替换 N12 组件间交错 Apply；本轮仅评估、未执行回滚。详见 `dev_plan/CDECR/CDECR_BULK_EPOCH_30_REAL_AB_ACCEPTANCE_REPORT_20260802.md`。
- Made the fixed-corpus Mention, Field, and N9 Gold evaluators honor the configured M4 provider through the production client factory. This removes their stale DashScope-only path, which returned provider arrearage even though workflow M2/M3/M4 had moved to the authorized DeepSeek provider; evaluator prompts, schemas, Gold, and scoring remain unchanged.
- Corrected the bulk dependency graph after a stopped diagnostic run exposed a 29-document false giant component: generic source-claim, same-company/family, and broad date-window equality no longer create Atomic scheduler edges. Atomic components now use exact identity plus candidate-like metric/period/lexical boundaries, while Package anchor/window contention is isolated to ordered N12 writer locks so it cannot suppress independent N9 work. The stopped partial Registry is retained as diagnostic evidence and was not used for acceptance metrics.
- Implemented CDECR bulk-epoch orchestration v1 for historical-news batches: persistent epoch/item checkpoints, conservative dependency-component execution, complete touched-Package N13 finalization independent of the last document, restart-safe finalized-epoch reuse, localized component failure and convergence handling, shared adaptive provider scheduling, and M1/M2/M3/M4 concurrency 8/24/24/12 with a one-second structured-request start gate. The evaluation CLI now uses the real bulk path for both first pass and idempotency replay; model prompts, business DTOs, N12 shadow mode, and LLM batch sizes remain unchanged.
- Enabled the dictionary N12 protocol by explicit user decision after adding three bounded mitigations: task-aware selection of the same four anchors and three Package representatives, compact high-confidence boundary-conflict hints, and one-task-only repair with conservative fallback. N9/N13 gates, candidate recall, batch size, output/reason contracts, and provider behavior remain unchanged; no real-model test was run in this change.

## 2026-07-10

- Implemented the intent-level Paper Trading revenue-audit vertical slice: immutable trade-time/source snapshots, three independent time bases, replaceable regular-session minute-bar providers, no-lookahead long/short calculations, adverse bilateral slippage, configurable virtual notional, versioned/idempotent SQLite persistence, weighted aggregates, partial/failure isolation, 18:00 ET independent scheduling, manual reruns, bounded Dashboard APIs, and a three-basis audit UI with coverage, trend, latency-loss, pagination, and detail views.
- Added unit/integration/query-plan coverage and real market-data capability evidence: the supplied Benzinga token returned HTTP 401 for Historical Bars, while the configured Twelve Data source returned a complete 390-bar AAPL regular session and is the current default without silent provider fallback.
- Added durable Supabase/Postgres persistence for dashboard model-usage cost audit data, including a compact RLS-protected `doxagent.model_usage_events` table, production repository wiring, indexed period queries, database-side detail pagination, and an idempotent SQLite backfill command.
- Reduced cost-audit database egress by excluding raw/JSON payloads, removing periodic cost-page refresh and synthetic cost SSE scans, bounding trend queries to ticker/time windows, and caching Overview daily cost summaries for five minutes.

## 2026-07-09

- Applied the Document 1 LLM context optimization plan across all three phases: scoped Build/Narrative task context, node-specific readable scopes, D1 snapshot visibility control, and compact Narrative global-research document buckets while retaining promoted expectation units.
- Optimized Document 2 LLM input context through Phase 3 of the Document2-vs-Document3 audit plan: removed workflow index/history fields from D2 task context, hid empty D2 context snapshots from model prompts, de-duplicated field-review inputs, replaced full top-level Document1 context packs with reviewer-scoped briefs, and made Document2 field-repair task headers avoid nested candidate/finding duplication.

## 2026-07-07

- Implemented the follow-up Supabase egress hardening pass: Blackboard runtime/dashboard/workflow paths now prefer lightweight document-bucket reads, active document-run bundle/context caching, targeted objection/delegation/working-memory writes, and targeted patch commit writes instead of full Blackboard run hydration; Document2 resolver/promotion and Known Events normalization now avoid loop-level full-run reads.
- Preserved the remote `doxagent-hk` dirty worktree on a `server-wip` branch before deployment recovery and tightened ignore rules for local temp snapshots, bundles, tarballs, and upload scratch directories so future server pulls do not pick up deployment artifacts.
- Removed previously tracked `.tmp*` deployment, pytest, cache, and scratch artifacts from Git tracking so they remain local-only under the tightened ignore rules.

## 2026-07-04

- Added a DoxAgent-only Supabase egress root-cause report that traces Shared Pooler usage to Dashboard Blackboard full-run read amplification, records Supabase table/query statistics plus remote SQLite/container evidence, and lays out a minimal optimization plan without changing production business flow.
- Expanded the Supabase egress report with a frontend-minimum-field backend read plan, Research/Strategy event-driven refresh requirements, a lightweight document revision probe, and the decision to remove Debug Viewer instead of keeping full-run debug APIs in the dashboard runtime.
- Fixed Dashboard Document 1/2/3 current-version semantics so real documents are bound to scheduler `document_run_id` instead of automatically following the newest Blackboard run, added a manual document activation API that updates scheduler state/reapplies monitoring config/audits the switch, exposed product-level version reason fields, and added frontend Markdown download from the rendered document display model.
- Added the production `runtime-scheduler` compose service as the formal Dashboard poll-and-consume worker, moved `monitoring-poller` behind the `legacy-debug` profile, updated deployment docs to build/start the scheduler with the dashboard, and exposed the current market session window in Overview so the former container-status KPI now shows `运行时段` or `盘后休眠`.
- Hardened Dashboard frontend deployment freshness by serving the SPA shell with `Cache-Control: no-store` while keeping hashed assets immutable, preventing stale `index.html` from pinning browsers to an old bundle after container rebuilds.
- Added dynamic Message Bus Channel Health rings that animate on each source's existing poll interval and reset on poll/config state changes, plus a 15-minute successful Supabase Dashboard auth cache keyed by bearer-token hash so repeated protected route checks do not re-hit Supabase while 401/403 results remain uncached.

